# Where crush finds skills (verified against crush 0.88.1 source).
# Global scan order - duplicates dedupe BY NAME, LAST occurrence wins:
#   ~/.config/crush/skills
#   ~/.config/agents/skills
#   ~/.agents/skills          <- canonical nix deploy (agent-skills.nix)
#   ~/.claude/skills          <- symlinks to canonical; wins ties harmlessly
# Project dirs are appended after globals (so they beat all of them):
#   .agents/skills  .crush/skills  .claude/skills  .cursor/skills
#   (working dir first, then git worktree root - NB upstream comment claims
#   local beats monorepo root, but last-wins makes the ROOT win)

# To run crush with ONLY one skills dir - CRUSH_SKILLS_DIR REPLACES the whole
# global list (it does not add to it). Project dirs still load:
CRUSH_SKILLS_DIR=~/skills-under-test crush

# To run crush with NO global skills at all:
CRUSH_SKILLS_DIR=/var/empty crush

# To disable specific skills instead (crush config option):
#   "options": { "disabled_skills": ["name", ...] }

# To check which copy of a duplicated skill won: it's the one from the
# LAST-scanned path above (e.g. ~/.claude/skills beats ~/.agents/skills).
